{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e292b525",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Code \n",
    "\n",
    "## Including Code and Code Snippets\n",
    "\n",
    "Quarto supports executable code, code examples, and syntax-highlighted snippets for a wide range of programming languages. This makes it ideal for creating teaching materials, laboratory manuals, lecture notes, and technical documentation.\n",
    "\n",
    "To show code as an example without executing it, set `#| eval: false`.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {.callout-warning}\n",
    "\n",
    "TODO: stop this accidentally echoing things back. See the page source to see the actual syntax.\n",
    "\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "    `````markdown "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "177e16c6",
   "metadata": {
    "md-indent": "    "
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#| eval: false\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "x = np.linspace(0, 10, 100)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7ab14fa5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "    `````\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "61dfaa28",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "#| eval: false\n",
    "\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "x = np.linspace(0, 10, 100)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "25bca980",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Running Code\n",
    "\n",
    "Executable code is placed inside a code chunk. Without the `#| eval: false` the code will run.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "```text"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "8c5730b6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Hello, world!\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Hello, world!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "831805c5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "b40da033",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Hello, world!\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Hello, world!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "12b255b0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Showing Output but Hiding Code\n",
    "You can run the code and display the output  but hide the code source from viewers with `#| echo: false`\n",
    "\n",
    "````text"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "9ebe42cf",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Only the output will appear.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: false\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Only the output will appear.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "25ad7842",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "````"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "f2aa3a39",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Only the output will appear.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: false\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Only the output will appear.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e107a1d0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Folding Long Code Blocks\n",
    "\n",
    "Long code examples can be collapsed to avoid cluttering the document."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "73e50aec",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "This code is initially hidden.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| code-fold: true\n",
    "#| code-summary: \"Show Python code\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"This code is initially hidden.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "17f10c0c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "::: {.callout-note}\n",
    "\n",
    "The folding code blocks are expanded in the static PDF output.\n",
    "\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "TODO ;;; note to encourage people to make sure lines aren't too long (as LaTeX output is not wrapped!)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "## Figures from code {#sec-code-figs}\n",
    "\n",
    "Figures generated from Python, R, or Julia code are **automatically** treated as figures. You can include the following (this generates a plot output and echos the original commands)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "fig-line-plot",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "application/pdf": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1650x1050 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| label: fig-line-plot\n",
    "#| fig-cap: A simple line plot\n",
    "#| fig-alt: Line graph showing values increasing and decreasing across four observations.\n",
    "\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.plot([1, 23, 2, 4])\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "75cefd57",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "::: {.callout}\n",
    "\n",
    "Often it's useful to add  `#| echo: false` at the start of the figure will make sure to not echo the code and only display the figure:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "fig-line-plot-noecho",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "application/pdf": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1650x1050 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#| echo: false\n",
    "#| label: fig-line-plot-noecho\n",
    "#| fig-cap: A simple line plot\n",
    "#| fig-alt: 'A simplified plot with the `#| echo: false` to not show the code'\n",
    "\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.plot([1, 23, 2, 4])\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3b6fc4d2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "## Global Code Options\n",
    "\n",
    "Chunk options can be applied to every code block using the document YAML.\n",
    "\n",
    "````markdown\n",
    "---\n",
    "execute:\n",
    "  echo: false\n",
    "  warning: false\n",
    "  message: false\n",
    "---\n",
    "````"
   ]
  }
 ],
